  "constraints": "* Input arrays/tensors are non-empty and well-formed\n* Floating point values are finite real numbers\n* Numerical operations must adhere to standard precision tolerances",
  "starterCode": "import pandas as pd\n\ndef pandas_aggregation_functions(records: list, group_col: str, value_col: str) -> dict:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Aggregation Functions** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\ndef pandas_aggregation_functions(records: list, group_col: str, value_col: str) -> dict:\n    df = pd.DataFrame(records)\n    return {fn: {str(k): round(float(v), 2) for k, v in df.groupby(group_col)[value_col].agg(fn).to_dict().items()} for fn in ['mean', 'sum', 'min', 'max']}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
